 pain.","They report she has become more irritable and withdrawn over the past 6 months.","Over this same period, she has experienced a rapid growth spurt, adding about 10 cm in height, and has developed acne and dark hair on her upper lip.","She has no breast development and has not begun menstruating.","Her external genitalia have appeared female since birth, although her parents recently noticed a 3\u20134 cm structure beneath the clitoral hood that they had never observed before."]},{"sid":59009,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Imperforate hymen with hematocolpos (diagnosed 2020-01-15)","- Primary amenorrhea","- Acne vulgaris","- Major depressive disorder","- History of inguinal hernia"]},{"sid":59010,"type":"psh","lines":["She has never undergone surgery"]},{"sid":59011,"type":"medications","lines":["Home Medications:","- Adapalene 0.1% topical gel Apply thin layer to face once daily at bedtime","- Ibuprofen 200mg by mouth every 6 hours as needed for pain","- Multivitamin One tablet by mouth daily"]},{"sid":59012,"type":"allergies","lines":["No known drug allergies"]},{"sid":59013,"type":"family_history","lines":["- Parents are first cousins once removed","- Maternal aunt with primary infertility","- No known family history of ambiguous genitalia"]},{"sid":59014,"type":"social_history","lines":["Smoking: Never. Alcohol: Never. Occupation: 8th grade student."]},{"sid":59015,"type":"vitals","lines":["Vital signs are normal."]},{"sid":59016,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["On physical exam, she is Tanner stage II for breast development, with Tanner stage III pubic hair.","No palpable gonads are noted in the labial folds or inguinal canals."]},{"sid":59017,"type":"imaging","lines":["A pelvic ultrasound reveals no uterus or ovaries."]}],"orders":[{"order_id":1825,"modality":"ultrasound","region":"pelvis","indication":"amenorrhea","provider":"Dr. Sarah Chen","priority":"routine","datetime":"2020-04-15","result_sid":59017}]},{"id":12233,"date":"2020-06-15","type":"outpatient","dept":"Endocrinology","attending":"Dr. James Peterson","cc":"Physical changes including facial acne, voice deepening, and increased muscle bulk without breast development","order":2,"method":"hybrid","question_ids":[6562],"sections":[{"sid":59018,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["Physical changes including facial acne, voice deepening, and increased muscle bulk without breast development"]},{"sid":59019,"type":"hpi","lines":["The patient returns for follow-up evaluation following prior consultation with Genetics and Obstetrics & Gynecology regarding primary amenorrhea and pubertal delay.","She has never had a menstrual period and has not developed breast tissue.","Over the past 6 months, the parents have noticed the development of facial acne, voice deepening, and increased muscle bulk."]},{"sid":59020,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Imperforate hymen with hematocolpos (diagnosed 2020-01-15)","- Androgen insensitivity syndrome (diagnosed 2020-04-15)","- Primary amenorrhea","- Acne vulgaris","- Major depressive disorder","- History of inguinal hernia"]},{"sid":59021,"type":"psh","lines":["- Neonatal inguinal hernia repair at age 2 months"]},{"sid":59022,"type":"medications","lines":["Home Medications:","- Adapalene 0.1% topical gel Apply thin layer to face once daily at bedtime","- Ibuprofen 200mg by mouth every 6 hours as needed for pain","- Multivitamin One tablet by mouth daily"]},{"sid":59023,"type":"allergies","lines":["No known drug allergies"]},{"sid":59024,"type":"family_history","lines":["- Parents are first cousins once removed","- Maternal aunt with primary infertility","- No known family history of ambiguous genitalia"]},{"sid":59025,"type":"social_history","lines":["Smoking: Never. Alcohol: Never. Occupation: 8th grade student."]},{"sid":59026,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["On exam, the child is tall and lean with mild facial hair, Tanner stage III pubic hair, and no breast development.","A firm structure measuring 3 cm is noted in the genital region, and the urethral opening is located at the base of this structure.","No scrotal sac is identifiable, and no gonads are palpable externally."]},{"sid":59027,"type":"labs","lines":["Serum testosterone is elevated, and LH is also elevated. Dihydrotestosterone (DHT) is low."]},{"sid":59028,"type":"imaging","lines":["Ultrasound reveals the absence of a uterus and ovaries."]},{"sid":59029,"type":"other_studies","lines":["Karyotype testing shows a 46XY genotype."]}],"orders":[{"order_id":1826,"modality":"ultrasound","region":"pelvis","indication":"primary amenorrhea","provider":"Dr. James Peterson","priority":"routine","datetime":"2020-06-15","result_sid":59028}]},{"id":12234,"date":"2021-04-15","type":"outpatient","dept":"Endocrinology","attending":"Dr. James Peterson","cc":"Progressive virilization with facial hair, deepening voice, and rapid growth velocity","order":3,"method":"hybrid","question_ids":[4234],"sections":[{"sid":59030,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["Progressive virilization with facial hair, deepening voice, and rapid growth velocity"]},{"sid":59031,"type":"hpi","lines":["The patient is a 14-year-old female with primary amenorrhea previously evaluated for imperforate hymen and androgen insensitivity syndrome who returns for evaluation of progressive physical changes.","Over the past few months, the parents have noticed increased muscle development, a deeper voice, and the emergence of facial hair along the upper lip.","The child has also grown approximately 4 inches in height in the past 4 months.","The parents are unsure whether this is typical puberty or something unusual.","The child denies any breast development and has not had any vaginal bleeding."]},{"sid":59032,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Imperforate hymen with hematocolpos (diagnosed 2020-01-15)","- Androgen insensitivity syndrome (diagnosed 2020-04-15)","- Primary amenorrhea","- Acne vulgaris","- Major depressive disorder","- Histor